<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Regulatory context</p>
    <h2>What the NPN means</h2>
    <p>The current Best Hydrate product page lists NPN 80118664. Health Canada explains that an NPN identifies a natural health product that has been authorized for sale in Canada under its labelled conditions of use.</p>
    <p>An NPN should not be stretched into a blanket claim that every proposed sports, medical or humanitarian use has been clinically proven. Product-specific claims should remain aligned with the authorized label and the evidence supporting the particular use being discussed.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Product boundary</span>
    <h3>Best Hydrate is not a World Health Organization therapeutic oral rehydration solution.</h3>
    <p>Some ingredients overlap with oral rehydration formulations, but therapeutic equivalence depends on composition, intended use and evidence.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

